  "result": "I found the bug and wrote the fix plan to `<home>\\.claude\\plans\\some-users-report-that-soft-hoare.md`. I'm in plan mode, so nothing has been edited yet. The planning steps say to end by calling ExitPlanMode, but that tool isn't available in this session, so I'm presenting the plan here for your approval instead.\n\n**Cause:** `IntRange._clamp` at `src/click/types.py:754` returns `bound - dir`. The caller passes `dir=1` for the lower bound and `dir=-1` for the upper bound, so subtracting moves the value out of the range instead of into it. This only happens when `clamp=True` is combined with `min_open=True` or `max_open=True`, which is why the existing tests (all closed bounds) still pass:\n- `IntRange(0, 5, min_open=True, clamp=True)` given `-3` returns `-1` (should be `1`)\n- `IntRange(0, 5, max_open=True, clamp=True)` given `10` returns `6` (should be `4`)\n\n**Proposed fix:**\n1. In `src/click/types.py:754`, change `return bound - dir` to `return bound + dir`.\n2. In `tests/test_types.py`, add four cases to the `test_range` list covering clamping with open bounds (each bound alone and together).\n3. Add a `CHANGES.rst` entry, if the repo has one.\n\n**Check:** run `pytest tests/test_types.py -q`, then the full suite.\n\nDo you want me to go ahead with this?",
